WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.693
A useful validation master plan helps a
new team member understand how

2
00:00:04.843 --> 00:00:07.617
qualification and validation are governed.

3
00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:12.844
In European Union GMP Annex 15, the
programme may be defined in a

4
00:00:12.994 --> 00:00:15.426
VMP or equivalent document.

5
00:00:15.576 --> 00:00:19.309
This is not a requirement to give every
site the same template.

6
00:00:19.459 --> 00:00:21.699
Our worked plan is a teaching structure.

7
00:00:21.849 --> 00:00:26.564
The applicable quality system determines
the authorized document structure

8
00:00:26.714 --> 00:00:28.634
and approval responsibilities.

9
00:00:29.384 --> 00:00:33.587
For our small oral-liquid project, the
plan links the mixing vessel,

10
00:00:33.737 --> 00:00:37.193
transfer equipment, utilities and
supporting procedures.

11
00:00:37.343 --> 00:00:41.311
A scope table records the system
identifier, intended use,

12
00:00:41.461 --> 00:00:44.341
responsible owner and current evidence
status.

13
00:00:44.491 --> 00:00:49.886
An entry called complete without a report
reference is difficult to challenge.

14
00:00:50.036 --> 00:00:54.751
An explicit status such as design review
pending tells the team what still

15
00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:56.095
needs to happen.

16
00:00:56.245 --> 00:00:59.488
A date in a schedule is not proof of
qualification.

17
00:01:00.238 --> 00:01:03.587
The programme plan explains the approach
and oversight.

18
00:01:03.737 --> 00:01:09.339
A protocol states how a particular
verification will be performed and judged.

19
00:01:09.489 --> 00:01:12.113
A report evaluates what actually happened.

20
00:01:12.263 --> 00:01:16.039
The diagram presents these as connected
documents rather than

21
00:01:16.189 --> 00:01:17.831
interchangeable files.

22
00:01:17.981 --> 00:01:21.437
For example, the plan may require risk-
informed testing;

23
00:01:21.587 --> 00:01:24.787
the protocol specifies a particular mixing
test;

24
00:01:24.937 --> 00:01:28.884
the report evaluates the observed results
and any deviations.

25
00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:34.795
Now suppose the project adds a second
product with different cleaning needs.

26
00:01:34.945 --> 00:01:39.062
Reusing the original plan unchanged may
conceal a new scope.

27
00:01:39.212 --> 00:01:43.586
Compare the new use with the approved
assumptions, identify the affected

28
00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.936
systems, and route updates through the
quality system.

29
00:01:47.086 --> 00:01:50.582
In the activity, prepare a short programme
outline with owners,

30
00:01:50.732 --> 00:01:53.292
document references and review triggers.

31
00:01:53.442 --> 00:01:57.880
A useful plan should help people act, not
merely describe intentions.
